# Generated from the OSRS Wiki page "Transcript:Mountain Daughter" by tools/quests/transcript_to_dialogue.py
# Hand edits (marked "# Authored (not Wiki)"): Fremennik-name placeholders -> {player}, the untemplated Asleif line restored, a {{tmissing}} reply and the post-quest Hamal replies authored. {{mes}} lines live in MountainDaughter.kt.
0	section	Entering the camp
0	section	Hamal's Daughter
1	action	If The Fremennik Trials has been completed, the player will introduce themselves with their Fremennik name, and Hamal will use that name in place of the player's username throughout the quest.
1	line	Hamal the Chieftain	Greetings, outerlander, I am Hamal. I am the chieftain of this tribe.
1	line	Player	And my name is {player}, honourable chieftain.
1	line	Hamal the Chieftain	Ah, an outerlander with manners.
1	line	Hamal the Chieftain	So tell me what you want from us.
1	option	Actually, I'm a Fremennik.
2	line	Player	Actually, I'm a Fremennik, not an outerlander.
2	line	Hamal the Chieftain	We are not Fremennik, outerlander.
2	line	Player	But you look like Fremennik!
2	line	Hamal the Chieftain	And you do not look like a Fremennik, but still claim to be one.
2	line	Hamal the Chieftain	But I will not deceive you. We were part of the Fremennik once, but left the village of Rellekka long ago.
2	option	So what are you doing up here?
3	action	below
2	option	That's fascinating.
3	line	Player	That's fascinating, but I'm afraid I have other things to do at the moment.
3	action	end
1	option	Why is everyone so hostile?
2	line	Player	Why is everyone being so hostile to me?
2	line	Hamal the Chieftain	We are a solitary group, outerlander, and have little experience or interest in outside contact.
2	line	Hamal the Chieftain	It is also our custom not to talk to outerlanders without my sanction. And I see no reason to sanction it for you.
2	option	So what are you doing up here?
3	line	Player	So what are you lot all doing up here in the mountains?
3	line	Hamal the Chieftain	We left Rellekka because we wanted to live closer to nature. We feel that the people of Rellekka have grown complacent and rely too much on their tools rather than their skill. And while they share our view on the sanctity
3	line	Hamal the Chieftain	of the runestones, they still employ and actively use magic.
3	line	Hamal the Chieftain	Their Seer is an affront to the gods!
3	cond	If The Fremennik Trials has been completed:
4	line	Player	And you haven't even seen what he did to his house!
4	line	Hamal the Chieftain	What?
3	line	Hamal the Chieftain	Anyway.
3	line	Hamal the Chieftain	We do not recognise the council of Rellekka and want nothing more to do with them. We live on rock and stone now, pure and hard.
3	line	Hamal the Chieftain	We move on to another part of the mountain slope when the rough land cannot sustain us anymore.
3	line	Hamal the Chieftain	That said, we have tarried at this location for too long and should be moving on.
3	line	Player	So why are you still here?
3	line	Hamal the Chieftain	For one thing, this side of the mountain is mostly free from the menace of the trolls and the delvings of the deformed dwarves.
3	line	Player	And?
3	line	Hamal the Chieftain	Well, you see...
3	line	Hamal the Chieftain	My daughter has gone missing. We have been looking for her and cannot go on without her.
3	option	I will search for her!
4	line	Player	A damsel in distress! I will search for her!
4	line	Hamal the Chieftain	Haha, you have spirit, {player}.
4	line	Hamal the Chieftain	But we do not employ outerlanders.
4	line	Player	You don't need to employ me! Just let me look for her.
4	line	Hamal the Chieftain	Hmmm.
4	line	Hamal the Chieftain	That seems acceptable to me. Very well, I will allow you to look for her.
4	line	Hamal the Chieftain	I will instruct my people to let you roam about the area freely, and give limited consent to them to talk to you.
4	line	Player	Great! I'll be back with her soon. Just wait here.
4	line	Hamal the Chieftain	Oh, I'll be waiting here alright.
4	action	end
3	option	I'm sorry to hear that.
4	line	Player	I'm sorry to hear that.
4	line	Hamal the Chieftain	We do not need your sympathy, outerlander.
4	action	end
3	option	Maybe the trolls got her?
4	line	Player	Maybe the trolls got her?
4	line	Hamal the Chieftain	Do not say such things in jest, outerlander.
4	line	Hamal the Chieftain	Besides, stealth and kidnapping is not their way.
4	option	I will search for her!
5	action	above
4	option	Forget it then.
5	line	Player	Forget it then, you can figure it out on your own.
5	action	end
2	option	Oh, I'll stop talking to you then.
3	line	Player	Oh, I'll stop talking to you then.
3	line	Hamal the Chieftain	As you wish, outerlander.
3	action	end
1	option	I'm looking for a quest!
2	line	Player	I'm looking for a quest! Do you have any for me?
2	line	Hamal the Chieftain	We do not employ outerlanders.
2	line	Player	Okay, I know the drill, where do I sign up for the trials to join your tribe?
2	line	Hamal the Chieftain	And we certainly don't let them join us!
2	action	end
0	section	Talking to Hamal again
1	option	Any idea on where I should start looking?
2	line	Player	Uhm... any idea on where I should start looking for your daughter?
2	line	Hamal the Chieftain	There is a large pool of water beyond the camp. She used to go there often, it was her favourite spot.
2	line	Hamal the Chieftain	Ragnar, her fiance, is probably there as well. I will give him my permission to talk to you.
2	action	end
1	option	What does your daughter look like?
2	line	Player	What does your daughter look like?
2	line	Hamal the Chieftain	She is the fairest maiden of all our tribe, and I daresay of all the northern lands. She has flowing black hair, and when last we saw her, she was wearing a brown dress.
2	line	Hamal the Chieftain	Perhaps you should speak to the man she is to marry, tribesman Ragnar. He can probably tell you more.
2	line	Hamal the Chieftain	You can find him out by the pool beyond the camp, where my daughter used to go so often.
2	action	end
