0	section	Guard by the entrance
1	line	Player	Can you come and help me? The chieftain's daughter-
1	line	Guard	No, outerlander, I'm guarding this mountain pass from trolls and inquisitive people like you.
1	line	Player	Doesn't look like you were very successful in the last regard.
1	line	Guard	If the chieftain would let me, I would correct that oversight.
1	action	end
0	section	Jokul
1	line	Player	Do you have any idea where the chieftain's daughter is?
1	line	Jokul	That's what we would all like to know.
1	action	end
0	section	Ragnar
1	line	Ragnar	So, you are the outerlander whom Hamal said would look for Asleif.
1	line	Player	Who?
1	line	Ragnar	You don't even know her name!
1	line	Ragnar	I am sorry outerlander, I have not spoken with your kind for a long time and I'm not feeling so well. You see, I was set to marry Asleif, the most beautiful woman ever to grace this world.
1	option	Do you have any idea where she might be?
2	line	Player	Do you have any idea where she might be?
2	line	Ragnar	She used to come here every day, you know, whenever our camp was set up in the vicinity. She would come to sing, her voice reflecting on the mountains and falling into the pool like sparkling silver. Sometimes I think I can hear her singing, but when I follow the sound around the pool I just end up here again.
2	line	Player	So... do you have any idea where she might be now?
2	line	Ragnar	We were supposed to meet here, at the tree by the pool. I think if I wait long enough maybe she will show up again.
2	line	Player	But... you don't actually have any idea where she is right at the moment?
2	line	Ragnar	If I knew I wouldn't be standing here, would I?
2	action	end
1	option	What do you mean, my kind?
3	line	Player	What do you mean, my kind?
3	line	Ragnar	You outerlanders with your fancy armour and your runestones and all your convenient little tools.
3	line	Player	Oh, that kind...
3	line	Player	What do you mean, my kind? I'm a Fremennik you know.
3	line	Ragnar	Yet you still use magic, I assume, and have little actual knowledge of the earth and the rock that you stand on every day.
3	line	Player	I suppose...
3	line	Ragnar	Then you are an ignorant, an insult to the gods... and an outerlander.
3	line	Player	Okay, okay, you made your point!
3	action	end
