0	section	Listening to the center shining pool
1	box	You can clearly hear the voice coming from the water now.
1	box	'{player}... {player}!'
1	line	Player	Er... yes, hello?
1	box	'Listen to me, {player}, listen to what I will say.'
1	option	I think I'm going mad.
2	line	Player	I think I'm going mad, I'm starting to hear things.
2	action	end
1	option	Hello! Who are you?
2	line	Player	Hello! Who are you? And where for that matter?
2	box	'I am all around you. I am the soft singing in the wind. I am the faint rippling of the water. I am the stone of the rocks around you.'
2	line	Player	Well, I suppose that answered both questions then.
2	box	'I am the voice of Asleif, daughter of Hamal, son of Wulfgard.'
2	line	Player	Wait, you're Asleif? I think I was looking for you! Where are you hiding?
2	box	'Asleif is no longer in your world, she dwells in the halls of her ancestors now.'
2	line	Player	But I thought you said you were Asleif?
2	box	'I am but the voice of her, an echo of the past, reflected on the water. A tiny part of her spirit.'
2	option	I think I'd better have a lie down.
3	line	Player	I think I'd better have a lie down, I'm starting to get a little dizzy.
3	action	end
2	option	So what exactly do you want from me?
3	line	Player	So what exactly do you want from me?
3	box	'I am greatly concerned for the people who were once my tribesmen. You must help me, {player}, for their current course will lead to their doom.'
3	line	Player	Er, I don't think they like the idea of me helping them.
3	box	'Listen to me, and judge then if you think yourself capable or not.'
3	box	'My people have, as is their way, isolated themselves from the rest of the world. There is no one for them to turn to in times of need.'
3	box	'Our tribesmen are the children of the Fremennik of Rellekka. The parting was a bitter affair and the two groups never forgave each other.'
3	box	'I ask you, {player}, to help bring these two people closer together again.'
3	option	That sounds like something I can do.
4	line	Player	All right, that sounds like something I can do.
4	box	'There is another thing, {player}, that I ask of you.'
4	line	Player	Yes?
4	box	'My father has not moved camp for far too long. There is very little food now for my people. You must find a new supply of food for them, for I fear the worst.'
4	option	I'll get right on it.
5	line	Player	I'll get right on it.
5	line	Player	So let's see, peace with Rellekka, and a new supply of food.'
5	box	'Thank you, {player}, and may the gods bless you on your journey.'
5	action	end
4	option	I'm not really a farmer.
5	line	Player	I'm sorry, but I'm not really a farmer. You'll have to find someone else.
5	box	'I am sad to hear that, {player}, but you must do what you think is right.'
5	action	end
3	option	I'm not really a diplomat.
4	line	Player	I'm sorry, but I'm not really a diplomat. You'll have to find someone else.
4	box	'I am sad to hear that, {player}, but you must do what you think is right.'
4	action	end
3	option	Don't tell me, there's an anthem involved?
4	line	Player	Don't tell me, there's an anthem involved?
4	box	'Your words are not clear to me. But please, try to find a way to bring our people closer together again.'
4	action	other
0	section	Talking to Asleif again
1	line	Player	Uh, hey, hello! Asleif spirit thing?
1	box	'Yes, {player}, what is it?'
1	line	Player	I forgot what you wanted me to do.
1	cond	If the player hasn't found a new supply of food yet:
2	box	'I wish that my people find a new supply of food.'
1	cond	If the player hasn't improved relations between the groups yet:
