0	section	Talking to him
1	line	Player	Errr... hello?
1	line	The Kendal	Who dares to disturb my slumber?
1	option	It's just me, no one special.
2	line	Player	It's just me, {player}, no one special.
2	line	The Kendal	Have you come, then, to pay your respects?
2	line	Player	How... exactly do I do that?
2	line	The Kendal	With your blood, mortal!
2	option	Time to go!
3	line	Player	Time to go, see you later!
3	line	The Kendal	Go now, mortal, but I'll be watching you!
3	action	end
2	option	You mean a sacrifice?
3	line	Player	You mean a sacrifice? Are you some kind of god?
3	line	The Kendal	I am the guardian of the mountain, the god of the northern lands. I move the earth and control the skies. I am the Kendal!
3	option	I seek your advice, oh great one!
4	line	Player	I seek your advice, oh great one.
4	line	Player	I seek the cowardly murderer of a young lady of a nearby clan of mountain people. Do you know where I can find this person?
4	line	The Kendal	I am not here to answer questions of such trivial nature! Go now before doom befalls you, mortal!
4	action	end
3	option	You look like you escaped from a fairground!
4	line	Player	You look like you escaped from a fairground!
4	line	The Kendal	I would not say such things if I were you, mortal!
4	action	end
3	option	You look like a man in a bearsuit!
4	line	Player	You look like a man in a bearsuit!
4	line	The Kendal	What did you say, mortal?
4	line	Player	I said, you look like a man wearing a bearsuit!
4	line	The Kendal	How did you figure that out? How did you know?
4	line	Player	I just said you looked like a man wearing a bearsuit, I didn't know you were!
4	action	Conversation will resume from here if aborted
4	line	Player	So what are you doing here, pretending to be a god?
4	line	The Kendal	Ah, the people that live in the mountains here, they are a superstitious lot. They fear few things, but magic and gods they're scared to death of.
4	line	The Kendal	So I took on the guise of one of their legends. It's a good way of being left alone.
4	line	Player	And do you leave them alone as well?
4	line	The Kendal	Ah, you're referring to the skeletons you see here? Yes, I did. Most of the time, at least. When there was no troll to be ambushed, and I had to eat...
4	line	Player	Did you kill a young lady, by the lake? Just recently?
4	line	The Kendal	Recently? Oh no, the entrance you came through has been blocked off for a good many years now. I've only seen trolls and the occasional stray dwarf since then, until you came along.
4	line	The Kendal	But yes, more than ten years ago, I did kill someone like that.
4	option	Oh, never mind then, that can't be right.
5	line	Player	Oh, never mind then, that can't be the person I'm looking for. I'll be off.
5	action	end
4	option	Can I see that corpse?
5	line	Player	Can I see that corpse? I'd like to make sure of something.
5	line	The Kendal	She is just over there, in the centre, with the dress. I did not eat her after I killed her, she was too beautiful for that.
5	line	The Kendal	I felt sorry for killing her, but by then it was already too late.
5	line	Player	Yes, she does match the description I was given, it is her after all!
5	option	Hand the body over to me!
6	line	Player	I demand that you hand the body over to me! I must return them to her father!
6	line	The Kendal	You demand nothing! You may have uncovered my disguise, but my claws can still tear you apart at will!
6	line	The Kendal	I will not allow you to leave!
6	action	The Kendal attacks the player
5	option	I humbly request to be given the remains.
6	line	Player	I humbly request to be given the remains, so I can return them to her father.
6	line	The Kendal	I cannot do that. If they knew I wasn't a god, and if her father knew I killed his daughter, the whole tribe would come in here at once and I'd be finished.
6	option	I will kill you myself!
7	line	Player	I will kill you myself!
7	line	The Kendal	Come and try!
7	action	The Kendal attacks the player
6	option	Never mind then, I'd better leave
7	line	The Kendal	I'm afraid I can't allow you to leave either. You cannot tell anyone about me.
7	action	The Kendal attacks the player
5	option	I think you're completely mad!
6	line	Player	I think you're completely mad, walking around in your silly bearsuit, killing innocent people!
6	line	The Kendal	And how is that very much different from you, walking around in silly suits of armour, killing everything that moves?
6	line	Player	Never mind.
6	action	end
1	option	It's me, of whom many legends are sung.
2	line	Player	It's {player}, of whom many legends are sung.
2	line	The Kendal	You are brave, to come into my cave and say a thing like that!
2	action	end
1	option	Slumber? You didn't seem to be sleeping.
2	line	Player	Slumber? You didn't seem to be sleeping.
2	line	The Kendal	Do not mock me, mortal!
2	action	end
