0	section	Talking to Ragnar again
1	line	Ragnar	I heard the news from Hamal, outerlander. Alas, I have known this had to be so for a long time, but Hamal just didn't want to listen.
1	line	Player	Uh huh.
1	line	Player	Well, Hamal asked me to bury her with some of her possessions. But he doesn't have any anymore.
1	line	Player	Do you have anything that may help?
1	line	Ragnar	I'm not altogether sure... I do have one thing that may be appropriate.
1	line	Ragnar	I was going to give her a necklace, when we were supposed to meet here many years ago.
1	line	Ragnar	I still have it, and since it was a gift for Asleif, technically it's hers.
1	line	Ragnar	Take it, outerlander, and bury it with her. It will be my parting gift.
1	action	
1	option	Thank you. I will make sure she's given a proper burial now.
2	action	end
1	option	You've been waiting to give it to her all that time?
2	line	Player	You've been waiting to give it to her all that time?
2	line	Ragnar	Oh yes... she is my only love, you see, and will be so forever.
2	line	Player	But that's ridiculous! Don't you ever go out and have some fun? What is wrong with you people!
2	line	Ragnar	I do not expect you to understand such things. But perhaps you will find your own love one day, and then you will remember these words.
