1	line	Player	So what are you all going to do now? Are you finally going to move to another location?
1	line	Hamal the Chieftain	No, I've decided to set up a permanent camp here.
1	line	Hamal the Chieftain	There is no need to move now with our new supply of food. Also, there is a protective spirit looking after us now.
1	option	Excuse me, have you seen my helmet?
# Authored (not Wiki): the transcript lists this option without its reply.
2	line	Player	Excuse me, have you seen my helmet? The bear one.
2	cond	If the player has lost the bearhead:
3	line	Hamal the Chieftain	One of my people found it by the lake. Here, outerlander, it is yours by right.
3	action	end
2	cond	If the player still has the bearhead:
3	line	Hamal the Chieftain	Is that not it you are carrying, outerlander?
3	action	end
1	option	Well, I must be off again.
# Authored (not Wiki): the transcript lists this option without its reply.
2	line	Player	Well, I must be off again.
2	line	Hamal the Chieftain	Go well, {player}. You will always be welcome in this camp.
2	action	end
1	option	What exactly happened to your daughter?
# Authored (not Wiki): the transcript lists this option without its reply.
2	line	Player	What exactly happened to your daughter?
2	line	Hamal the Chieftain	The bearman took her from the lake while she sang, fourteen years ago. We thought the Kendal had claimed her and dared not look.
2	line	Hamal the Chieftain	Now she rests on the island, and her voice watches over us still.
2	action	end
1	option	I thought you didn't believe in magic?
# Authored (not Wiki): the transcript lists this option without its reply.
2	line	Player	I thought you didn't believe in magic?
2	line	Hamal the Chieftain	We do not use magic, outerlander. But the spirits of our ancestors are no runestone trickery. They are part of the earth and the rock, as we are.
2	action	end
1	option	I think you're all mad.
# Authored (not Wiki): the transcript lists this option without its reply.
2	line	Player	I think you're all mad.
2	line	Hamal the Chieftain	Perhaps we are, outerlander. But we are free, and now we are fed. That is enough for us.
2	action	end
